Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: The Left Margin Moves After Eight Bars

Story & Context: During the first proof-pull rehearsal, Ilze notices that an alignment mark has been drawn slightly too far inward on the left side of the page. Malik turns the mistake into an arrangement rule: the main clap must shift later in the bar after every eight-bar cycle while the kokle ostinato remains unchanged. Ilze plays a narrow Dorian figure built from one bass string and three upper notes, making the rhythmic displacement increasingly obvious without changing the harmony.

Mara answers every second shifted clap with a single felt-damped toy-piano note. Edgars waits until the fourth cycle before entering with a low bass-clarinet tone that bends upward into the kokle’s pedal note. As the track develops, Malik removes one kick whenever the clap reaches its latest position, creating a groove that seems to lean sideways rather than accelerate.

The final eight bars return the clap to its original timing, but Ilze moves the kokle bass note for the first time, making the restored rhythm feel newly unstable.

