Track 2: Registration Pin Under the Third Dyad

Story & Context: Mara drops a small metal registration pin onto the toy piano during setup and discovers that it creates a short metallic rattle when one specific dyad is played. Rather than remove it, she places the pin deliberately under the instrument and builds the track around the accidental resonance.

Ilze performs muted kokle plucks in two-note cells, leaving more silence than in the first track. Malik builds a rolling UK funky groove from kick, low tom, clap, and proof-frame knock, but removes the expected rimshot whenever Mara plays the rattling dyad. Edgars answers only those empty spaces with short bass-clarinet key-noise bursts and underblown notes.

Halfway through, Mara removes the pin. The dyad becomes suddenly clean and almost too polite. The ensemble leaves the cleaner sound exposed for sixteen bars before replacing the pin and restoring the unstable rattle for the final section.

